From: Fix GLES 2.0 crash in glGetStringi
Subject: Replace NULL glGetStringi with safe stub on GLES 2.0 drivers

On GLES 2.0 drivers (e.g. Vivante GC NanoUltra on i.MX8MM),
glGetStringi is not available (it requires GLES 3.0+). Chromium's
GL dispatch table gets a NULL function pointer from eglGetProcAddress.
Various code paths call it without checking, causing a SIGSEGV.

Previous approaches (guarding individual call sites in GLApiBase and
RealGLApi) failed because Chromium is built with thin LTO, which
inlines functions across compilation units. Stale inlined copies in
other object files bypass the guards.

Fix by replacing the NULL function pointer with a safe stub at
initialization time in DriverGL::InitializeStaticBindings(). The stub
simply returns nullptr. Since the function pointer is never NULL,
ALL code paths are safe regardless of LTO inlining.

Tested on: NXP i.MX8MM EVK with Chromium 129.0.6668.100
(Vivante GC NanoUltra, GLES 2.0 only)

Upstream-Status: Submitted [https://crbug.com]

---

--- a/ui/gl/gl_bindings_autogen_gl.cc
+++ b/ui/gl/gl_bindings_autogen_gl.cc
@@ -25,6 +25,14 @@

 namespace gl {

+// Safe stub for glGetStringi on GLES 2.0 drivers where the real function
+// is not available (requires GLES 3.0+). Prevents NULL pointer crashes
+// throughout all code paths, including LTO-inlined callers.
+static const GLubyte* GL_BINDING_CALL glGetStringiStub(GLenum name,
+                                                       GLuint index) {
+  return nullptr;
+}
+
 void DriverGL::InitializeStaticBindings() {
   // Ensure struct has been zero-initialized.
   char* this_bytes = reinterpret_cast<char*>(this);
@@ -336,6 +344,15 @@
       GetGLProcAddress("glVertexAttribPointer"));
   fn.glViewportFn =
       reinterpret_cast<glViewportProc>(GetGLProcAddress("glViewport"));
+
+  // Replace NULL glGetStringi with a safe stub on GLES 2.0 drivers.
+  // The stub returns nullptr, which is safe for all callers.
+  // This MUST be done here (at init time) rather than at call sites,
+  // because LTO may inline callers across compilation units.
+  if (!fn.glGetStringiFn) {
+    fn.glGetStringiFn =
+        reinterpret_cast<glGetStringiProc>(glGetStringiStub);
+  }
 }

 void DriverGL::InitializeDynamicBindings(const GLVersionInfo* ver,

